\subsection{LSP coexistence design}\label{lsp-coexistence-design}

Current state per language, from the file:

\begin{itemize}
\tightlist
\item
  Python (regular): lsp-mode with \texttt{lsp-pyright}, using
  \texttt{basedpyright} (\texttt{lsp-pyright-langserver-command}). This
  matches the assumption.
\item
  Python (notebooks): Eglot, selected by \texttt{h7/python-lsp-switch}.
\item
  R: no LSP client is configured. \texttt{ess} provides its own
  completion and help. Adding an Eglot entry for the
  \texttt{languageserver} package is optional and would need a
  container-aware guard.
\item
  Julia: Eglot through \texttt{eglot-jl} (see DUP-07).
  \texttt{lsp-julia} is configured but never started.
\end{itemize}

The target design is a single dispatcher (ENH-01). It is the only code
that starts a client, it runs after directory-local variables are known,
and it is driven by this precedence:

\begin{itemize}
\tightlist
\item
  An explicit \texttt{h7/python-lsp-backend} value (buffer, file or
  directory local) wins.
\item
  Otherwise a \texttt{notebooks} path component selects Eglot.
\item
  Otherwise a \texttt{\#\ \%\%} marker in the first 64 KiB selects
  Eglot.
\item
  Otherwise lsp-mode is used.
\end{itemize}

Interactions per client are summarised below.

\begin{longtable}[]{@{}lll@{}}
\toprule\noalign{}
Concern & lsp-mode buffer & Eglot buffer \\
\midrule\noalign{}
\endhead
\bottomrule\noalign{}
\endlastfoot
Diagnostics & Flycheck & Flymake \\
Completion & corfu with lsp capf & corfu with eglot capf \\
Formatting & \texttt{ruff-format} on save & manual
\texttt{eglot-format} \\
Eldoc & eldoc and lsp-ui-doc & eldoc only \\
Xref & lsp xref backend & eglot xref backend \\
Prefix & \texttt{C-c\ L} (ENH-08) & \texttt{C-c\ L} (ENH-08) \\
\end{longtable}

