\subsection{site-boot.el and the unloaded
files}\label{site-bootel-and-the-unloaded-files}

\texttt{site-boot.el} itself was not provided, so only its documented
load order can be judged.

\begin{itemize}
\tightlist
\item
  \texttt{site-pkgs} loads before \texttt{site-func}, \texttt{site-cust}
  and \texttt{site-keys}. Helpers called while \texttt{site-pkgs} loads
  (\texttt{h7/use-vertico}, \texttt{h7/use-py-jupyter}) must be defined
  in \texttt{site-pref} or \texttt{site-conf}. Check with
  \texttt{rg\ -n\ "defun\ h7/use-"\ \textasciitilde{}/.emacs-site/*.el}.
  Not verifiable from the provided files.
\item
  \texttt{site-cust} loads after \texttt{site-pkgs}, so values stored by
  Customize can override \texttt{:custom} settings made in this file.
\item
  \texttt{site-keys} loads last among the key files, so its
  \texttt{global-set-key} forms win over \texttt{:bind} entries here
  (for example \texttt{C-SPC}).
\item
  Do not load another file by name from \texttt{site-boot.el} without a
  \texttt{load} fallback; a missing file should warn, not abort startup.
  Not verifiable from the provided files.
\end{itemize}

