\section{Executive Summary}\label{executive-summary-1}

An audit of \texttt{site-pkgs.org} against GNU Emacs 32.0.50 reveals a
long-lived configuration that combines modern completion and navigation
paradigms (\texttt{vertico}, \texttt{consult}, \texttt{corfu},
\texttt{embark}, \texttt{orderless}) with legacy scaffolding
(\texttt{company}, \texttt{flycheck}, \texttt{etags}, unused elpa
bootstrapping blocks). While the underlying Org-babel literate structure
is robust, several duplicated completion stacks, conflicting linter
backends (\texttt{flycheck} vs \texttt{flymake}), and syntax errors in
Python buffer hooks require remediation.

This document delivers an inventory classification, structured finding
records (\texttt{OBS-}, \texttt{DUP-}, \texttt{ENH-}, \texttt{DEF-}), a
deterministic Python LSP/Eglot coexistence design for Jupyter notebooks
versus standard scripts, actionable enhancement snippets with rollback
instructions, deferred items, and a complete package inventory.

