\subsubsection{\texorpdfstring{\textbf{Recommended ownership
model}}{Recommended ownership model}}\label{recommended-ownership-model}

This is the intended architecture, not a claim that the current
configuration already implements it.

\begin{verbatim}
                  Python file opened
                         |
                         v
              Process directory locals
                         |
                         v
             Inspect notebook selection
                         |
             +-----------+-----------+
             |                       |
             v                       v
     Ordinary Python          Notebook Python
             |                       |
             v                       v
         lsp-mode                  Eglot
             |                       |
             v                       v
          Flycheck                Flymake
             |                       |
             +-----------+-----------+
                         |
                         v
                 Shared interfaces
              Corfu / CAPF / ElDoc
                    Xref
\end{verbatim}

\begin{longtable}[]{@{}lll@{}}
\toprule\noalign{}
Responsibility & Ordinary Python & Notebook Python \\
\midrule\noalign{}
\endhead
\bottomrule\noalign{}
\endlastfoot
LSP client & \texttt{lsp-mode} & Eglot \\
Language server & basedpyright & Explicitly verify Eglot server
command \\
Ruff diagnostics & LSP integration & Eglot server integration \\
Diagnostics frontend & Flycheck & Flymake \\
Completion frontend & Corfu & Corfu \\
Completion source & LSP CAPF & Eglot CAPF \\
Formatting & Ruff on save & Explicit/manual formatting \\
Documentation & ElDoc / LSP UI & ElDoc \\
Navigation & Xref & Xref \\
Project navigation & Consult / project.el & Consult / project.el \\
\end{longtable}

This division is technically coherent because both clients use the
standard Emacs interfaces for completion, documentation and navigation.
Eglot\textquotesingle s diagnostic backend is Flymake; \texttt{lsp-mode}
supports Flycheck.\footnote{\href{https://github.com/emacs-lsp/lsp-mode?utm_source=chatgpt.com}{lsp-mode
  — official project documentation}.}

\textbf{Important:} The actual Eglot server configuration still needs
independent verification. Its comment describes
\texttt{basedpyright-langserver} and Ruff, but the executable
configuration currently specifies:

\begin{verbatim}
(python-ts-mode . ("rass"
                   "--" "ty" "server"
                   "--" "ruff" "server"))
\end{verbatim}

That is not the server command described in the surrounding comments. I
would not replace it blindly without confirming the intended
\texttt{rass} executable and its multi-server protocol.

There is a second mismatch: \texttt{lsp-pyright} is configured to
execute \texttt{basedpyright}, but \texttt{h7/lsp-setup} calls
\texttt{lsp-install-server} for \texttt{pyright}. These should be
reconciled.

