\subsection{\texorpdfstring{\textbf{6.3 External configuration
dependencies}}{6.3 External configuration dependencies}}\label{63-external-configuration-dependencies}

Several identifiers referenced in \texttt{site-pkgs.org} are not defined
in the supplied file:

\begin{itemize}
\tightlist
\item
  \texttt{h7/use-vertico}
\item
  \texttt{h7/use-py-jupyter}
\item
  \texttt{h7/org-mode-setup}
\item
  \texttt{emacs-d}
\item
  \texttt{ha-leader}
\end{itemize}

Their definitions and load order are not verifiable from the provided
files.

This matters because \texttt{site-boot.el} loads \texttt{site-pkgs}
before \texttt{site-func}, \texttt{site-cust} and the later modules.

Any helper evaluated immediately by \texttt{site-pkgs} must already be
defined in \texttt{site-pref}, \texttt{site-conf} or the local
overrides. A definition appearing only in \texttt{site-func} would be
too late.

In particular, \texttt{h7/use-vertico} is called immediately in the
Vertico configuration, so its definition must exist before
\texttt{site-pkgs} is evaluated.

