\section{\texorpdfstring{\textbf{9.
References}}{9. References}}\label{9-references}

The following documentation supports the recommendations.
Package-specific availability and behaviour should still be checked
against the versions actually installed in your Emacs 32 distribution.

\textbf{Final assessment:} I would not undertake a wholesale rewrite.
The existing configuration already has most of the components needed for
a modern Emacs development environment.

I would implement the Python LSP ownership changes first, then remove
the legacy completion and project-management overlaps, and finally
address startup and keymap cleanup.

One important limitation remains: \texttt{site-boot.el},
\texttt{site-keys.el} and the other loaded modules were not supplied as
source files. Their actual runtime interactions, helper definitions and
load-order dependencies cannot be certified by this audit. The keymap
scan provides supplementary evidence, but it is not a substitute for
inspecting the complete configuration.

The safest next step is to make the Python LSP changes in isolation,
tangle \texttt{site-pkgs.org}, and test ordinary \texttt{.py} files and
percent-format notebooks under both \texttt{python-mode} and
\texttt{python-ts-mode} before proceeding with the broader cleanup.

