\section{Executive Summary}\label{executive-summary-3}

The configuration is a large, long-lived \texttt{use-package} codebase
that has already adopted many modern tools (\texttt{vertico},
\texttt{consult}, \texttt{embark}, \texttt{corfu}, \texttt{cape},
\texttt{treesit-auto}, \texttt{eglot}). However, it still carries legacy
layers that create real conflicts: \textbf{\texttt{company} and
\texttt{corfu} compete for in-buffer completion},
\textbf{\texttt{flycheck} and \texttt{flymake} (via Eglot) compete for
diagnostics}, and \textbf{both \texttt{lsp-mode} and \texttt{eglot} are
configured for Python and Julia without a reliable per-buffer switch}. A
notebook hook is syntactically broken. \texttt{ace-jump-mode},
\texttt{undo-tree}, \texttt{diminish}, and \texttt{flyspell} have modern
replacements already present or clearly preferred. The global keymap
scan shows extensive use of \texttt{global-set-key} in
\texttt{site-keys.el}, but that file was not provided, so global
keybinding conflicts cannot be fully verified.

