\section{Executive Summary /k}\label{executive-summary-k}

The configuration is in better shape than its age suggests: the
vertico/consult/embark/corfu stack is present and mostly wired
correctly, and the lsp-mode/eglot coexistence scaffolding already
exists. The main problems are: (1) several \emph{active} legacy packages
that duplicate or fight the target stack (company, undo-tree,
projectile, treemacs suite, flyspell+jinx); (2) one genuinely dangerous
bug — a \texttt{cond} form inside a \texttt{:custom} block in
\texttt{lang-python.mode}; (3) a broken eglot activation path
(\texttt{derived-mode-p\ \textquotesingle{}python-mode} fails in
\texttt{python-ts-mode}, so \texttt{h7/python-use-eglot} errors in
exactly the buffers it targets); (4) non-deterministic notebook
detection (substring \texttt{"notebooks"}); and (5) a large tail of
disabled/commented blocks from the 1990s–2000s and five files that
\texttt{site-boot.el} never loads, two of which (\texttt{site-init.el})
contain live-looking duplicate keybindings.

Highest priorities: ENH-01 (broken \texttt{:custom}), ENH-02 (LSP
router), ENH-06/ENH-07 (broken bindings and typos), DUP-02 (three
packages claiming \texttt{.md}), ENH-08 (startup hygiene).

