\section{Additional Notes /k}\label{additional-notes-k}

\begin{itemize}
\tightlist
\item
  The pasted file ends with
  \texttt{Wrong\ type\ argument:\ integer-or-marker-p,\ nil}. This
  cannot be attributed from the provided files. Most plausible
  candidates given this audit: the malformed \texttt{:custom} entries
  (ENH-01, ENH-07), the \texttt{hydra-of-hydras}/\texttt{hydra-*}
  definitions, or dashboard startup. Diagnose with
  \texttt{emacs\ -\/-debug-init} and, if needed, bisect by tangling
  halves of \texttt{site-pkgs.org}.
\item
  Load-order hazard: \texttt{site-boot.el} loads \texttt{site-pkgs}
  \emph{before} \texttt{site-func} and \texttt{site-keys}, yet
  \texttt{site-pkgs} calls at load time \texttt{h7/use-vertico} (twice,
  in "Vertico*/begin/end"), \texttt{h7/use-pdf-tools},
  \texttt{h7/use-py-jupyter}, \texttt{h7/var-*}, \texttt{emacs-d},
  \texttt{ha-leader}, and references \texttt{joe-*},
  \texttt{scroll-down-one}, \texttt{xah-*}, \texttt{toggle-*}. These
  must be defined in \texttt{site-pref}/\texttt{site-conf} to be safe —
  not verifiable from the provided files. Consider moving all
  \texttt{h7/*} helper definitions into the "General" section of this
  file so the dependency direction is self-contained.
\item
  \texttt{:no-require} appears in \texttt{use-package\ citar} and
  \texttt{use-package\ citar-embark}; it is not a standard use-package
  keyword (needs verification how your build treats unknown keywords —
  ignored or error). Replace with \texttt{:defer\ t} if in doubt.
\item
  \texttt{(setq\ org-element-use-cache\ nil)} disables org-element
  caching globally for an imenu issue that is likely stale on Emacs 32 —
  re-test with it removed; org startup will get noticeably faster on
  large files.
\item
  \texttt{server-use-tcp\ t} with a fixed port 60321 is fine on one
  machine but will collide if two Emacsen start on the same host
  (notably WSL + Windows, or Podman containers sharing the network
  namespace). Consider a per-UID port or unix sockets where available.
\item
  The REFS "GLOBAL" table documents intended bindings; after
  ENH-06/ENH-10 the live config matches it (modulo eshell, deferred).
\end{itemize}

