\section{1. Executive summary}\label{1-executive-summary-1}

The configuration is a healthy modern core (vertico, consult, embark,
orderless, corfu, cape, lsp-mode, eglot, treesit-auto) wrapped in
roughly two decades of accumulated dead weight: 74 of 252
\texttt{use-package} forms are disabled or dead, several active blocks
duplicate each other, and the lsp-mode/eglot per-buffer switching
mechanism contains four defects that prevent it from working
deterministically. The highest priority items are the Python LSP
dispatcher redesign (DUP-03), the broken eglot server specification
(ENH-04), and \texttt{markdown-ts-mode\ :ensure\ t} on a build where the
mode is built-in (OBS-18).

Findings are backed only by the attached \texttt{site-pkgs.org} and the
\texttt{rg} keymap scan. Other \texttt{site-*.el} files were not
provided; where a finding depends on them, it is marked "not verifiable
from the provided files".

