\section{Main changes applied}\label{main-changes-applied}

\subsection{Completion and search}\label{completion-and-search}

\begin{itemize}
\tightlist
\item
  Removed Auto-Complete and IDO; retained Corfu +
  Vertico/Orderless/Marginalia/Consult.
\item
  Removed Company as a completion UI, including Company-posframe/global
  activation. Company remains deferred only as a provider for legacy
  Ansible, Terraform and AUCTeX backends, adapted through
  Cape\textquotesingle s CAPF bridge.
\item
  Removed unused ace-jump-mode and the unbound Avy declaration.
\item
  Removed the redundant ack/ag/deadgrep/rg search frontends and later
  grep key overrides; Consult + ripgrep is the primary search path.
  \texttt{wgrep} remains for editing grep results.
\item
  Removed the unused deferred \texttt{regex-tool} declaration.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Project and UI cleanup}\label{project-and-ui-cleanup}

\begin{itemize}
\tightlist
\item
  \texttt{project.el} is the primary project interface: the project
  Hydra and Dashboard backend now use it, and the Python Behave helper
  prefers it.
\item
  Projectile remains deferred as a compatibility layer for
  terminal/Eshell integrations and existing commands; it is not globally
  enabled. \texttt{consult-projectile} and \texttt{treemacs-projectile}
  were removed.
\item
  Removed Minions; Mood-Line is the only active modeline implementation.
  Delight remains complementary.
\item
  Removed the empty Fontaine section.
\item
  Removed external Which-Key setup and enabled Emacs\textquotesingle{}
  built-in Which-Key.
\item
  Replaced stale IDO/Helm buffer Hydra commands with
  \texttt{consult-buffer} and \texttt{ibuffer}.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{\texorpdfstring{Folding and keymaps in
\texttt{site-pkgs.org}}{Folding and keymaps in site-pkgs.org}}\label{folding-and-keymaps-in-site-pkgsorg}

\begin{itemize}
\tightlist
\item
  Removed Kirigami, Savefold, Vimish-Fold and their dead configuration.
\item
  Retained Tree-sitter folding, Outline/outline-indent and Hideshow; the
  fold Hydra now uses those commands.
\item
  Moved Treemacs to \texttt{C-c\ T}; Python pytest keeps the lowercase
  \texttt{C-c\ t} prefix. These are case-distinct key sequences, not a
  direct conflict.
\item
  Moved the lsp-mode prefix to \texttt{C-c\ L}, preserving
  \texttt{C-c\ l} for the Python backend switcher.
\item
  Removed duplicate ESS assignments: \texttt{M-c\ M-j},
  \texttt{M-c\ M-r} and \texttt{M-c\ M-e} each now have one binding; the
  displaced commands use \texttt{M-c\ M-u} and \texttt{M-c\ M-E}.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Python and LSP}\label{python-and-lsp}

\begin{itemize}
\tightlist
\item
  Removed Elpy, EIN and pyvenv-auto. \texttt{uv-mode} + PET is the
  environment workflow.
\item
  Fixed the Python \texttt{:custom}/\texttt{cond} misuse by moving
  interpreter selection to \texttt{:init}.
\item
  Consolidated Flycheck, lsp-mode, Eglot, lsp-ui, Consult-LSP and
  lsp-treemacs into one LSP configuration; removed the second LSP block
  and its unconditional Python \texttt{lsp-deferred} hooks.
\item
  Added a buffer-local dispatcher on \texttt{hack-local-variables-hook},
  so \texttt{.dir-locals.el} overrides are read before client selection.
  It stops any existing client before starting exactly one:

  \begin{itemize}
  \tightlist
  \item
    ordinary Python buffers: lsp-mode + basedpyright + Flycheck + Ruff
    format-on-save;
  \item
    percent-format files under a \texttt{notebooks} directory: Eglot +
    basedpyright + Flymake, without Ruff format-on-save.
  \end{itemize}
\item
  Both \texttt{python-mode} and \texttt{python-ts-mode} use the same
  Eglot basedpyright mapping. \texttt{h7/python-lsp-backend} is a safe
  local variable (\texttt{lsp} or \texttt{eglot}) for explicit
  overrides.
\item
  Replaced the unknown \texttt{rass} server command with the explicit
  \texttt{basedpyright-langserver\ -\/-stdio} command. Ruff is retained
  as the formatter, not configured as a second Eglot language server.
\item
  \texttt{h7/lsp-setup} now prints
  \texttt{uv\ tool\ install\ basedpyright} instead of asking lsp-mode to
  install Microsoft\textquotesingle s Pyright.
\item
  Flycheck is enabled for lsp-mode buffers; the dispatcher disables it
  for Eglot buffers, where Flymake is used.
\item
  Julia retains Eglot-jl; its extended startup timeout is buffer-local.
  The dormant lsp-julia declaration was removed. R remains ESS-based; no
  R LSP server is configured.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Other correctness and startup
changes}\label{other-correctness-and-startup-changes}

\begin{itemize}
\tightlist
\item
  Fixed the malformed \texttt{hl-todo} \texttt{:custom} entries.
\item
  Replaced destructive assignment to \texttt{major-mode-remap-alist}
  with \texttt{add-to-list}.
\item
  Removed redundant \texttt{package-initialize}, old req-package/Quelpa
  bootstrap code and the invalid \texttt{:ensure\ f} system-package
  declaration. Emacs\textquotesingle{} built-in \texttt{use-package} and
  normal package activation are used.
\item
  Raised GC threshold only during startup and restored it to 16 MiB in
  \texttt{emacs-startup-hook}.
\item
  Switched Org to the Emacs-bundled version (\texttt{:ensure\ nil})
  rather than installing a second ELPA copy.
\item
  Removed disabled Org-ref/Org-roam integrations; Citar and Denote
  remain.
\item
  Removed unactivated ef-themes and other unused deferred declarations.
\item
  Added safe defaults for helper functions that were referenced before
