\subsection{\texorpdfstring{\texttt{site-keys.el} (public repository
\texttt{master})}{site-keys.el (public repository master)}}\label{site-keysel-public-repository-master}

\begin{itemize}
\tightlist
\item
  \textbf{\texttt{C-f}} is bound to \texttt{consult-line}, overriding
  Emacs\textquotesingle{} normal \texttt{forward-char}. It is also
  redundant with the existing Consult search binding (\texttt{M-s\ l}).
  Consider removing this global override to restore normal cursor
  movement.
\item
  \textbf{\texttt{C-t}} is bound to \texttt{forward-char}, overriding
  Emacs\textquotesingle{} normal \texttt{transpose-chars}. This is
  separate from \texttt{C-c\ t} (Python pytest).
\item
  \textbf{\texttt{C-,\ ,} and \texttt{C-,\ C-,}} both call
  \texttt{ranger}. The Ranger declaration was disabled and has been
  removed from the refactored \texttt{site-pkgs.org}; these two keys are
  now unresolved. Rebind to \texttt{project-dired}, \texttt{dired-jump}
  or another active file/project command.
\item
  \textbf{F4 family:} plain F4 calls \texttt{vimish-fold-toggle};
  Ctrl-F4 calls \texttt{vimish-fold-refold-all-from-marks};
  Ctrl-Shift-F4 calls \texttt{vimish-fold-unfold-all}; Meta-Shift-F4
  calls \texttt{vimish-fold}. Those commands are no longer provided by
  the active configuration. Shift-F4 (\texttt{hydra-fold/body}) remains
  valid because the Hydra was rewritten to use
  Outline/Hideshow/Tree-sitter folding. Rebind the other F4 variants to
  that Hydra or to the new folding commands.
\item
  \textbf{Numeric keypad:} \texttt{kp-enter} and \texttt{kp-insert} both
  call \texttt{yank}. This is a redundant alias rather than a functional
  conflict; retain it if the duplication is intentional. The modified
  keypad rectangle commands are otherwise internally consistent.
\item
  \textbf{F12} calls \texttt{h7/make-note-frame}. Its definition was not
  in the supplied \texttt{site-pkgs.org} or keymap scan; verify that an
  active earlier-loaded file defines it.
\end{itemize}

The current public source does \textbf{not} bind Ctrl-F4 to a Helm
command: it binds \texttt{vimish-fold-refold-all-from-marks}. The actual
key assignments are visible in the repository\textquotesingle s
\href{https://github.com/hute37/emacs-site/blob/master/site-keys.el}{\texttt{site-keys.el}},
notably the C-comma map, F4 group, C-f/C-t assignments and keypad
bindings.

