\texttt{site-load.el} duplicates a very large legacy binding set;
because it is not loaded, its bindings are latent rather than active
conflicts.

\begin{itemize}
\item
  Key: \texttt{C-c\ t} in \texttt{site-pkgs.org}:
  \texttt{gtags-find-rtag} is bound under the disabled \texttt{gtags}
  block, while active \texttt{python-pytest} binds the \texttt{C-c\ t}
  prefix; remove the Gtags bindings with the Gtags block or move pytest
  to another prefix.
\item
  Key: \texttt{C-c\ f} in \texttt{site-pkgs.org}: \texttt{treemacs}
  binds \texttt{C-c\ f}, while \texttt{fontaine-set-preset} also binds
  \texttt{C-c\ f}; retain Treemacs and move Fontaine to an unused prefix
  such as \texttt{C-c\ F}.
